# infra/secrets/ch_password.example — the shape, never a live credential.
#
# Copy to `infra/secrets/ch_password` (gitignored) and replace the line below
# with the password for the ClickHouse user named by `clickhouse.user`. The
# collector reads the file named by `clickhouse.password_file` at startup and
# trims exactly one trailing newline, so a file ending in a newline and one
# that does not yield the same credential.
#
# Everything above this line is part of the example, not the format: the real
# file holds ONE line and nothing else. Mount it `0400`, owned by the
# container's non-root user; deployed, it is a projected volume from a managed
# secret store, never an env var, never a build arg, never a value in a Compose
# file (NFR-10, SPEC §14.2).
#
# Only `*.example` may live in this directory — scripts/ci/invariants.d/
# 04-no-plaintext-secrets.sh fails the build on anything else.
replace-me
